meta {
  name: Create Room
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/rooms
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.getStatus() === 201) {
    bru.setEnvVar("roomId", res.getBody().id);
  }
}

docs {
  # Create Room

  The caller (Player 1 by default) becomes the room's owner and its first
  seated player. Captures the new room's id into `roomId` for the WS
  requests and for "Close Room" below.

  A player may be seated in at most one room at a time — this call also
  blocks that player's withdrawals until the room closes.

  **Expected success**: `201` with the room summary
  `{id, owner_id, status: "open", current_round: 0, max_rounds: 10,
  player_count: 1, max_players: 6, created_at}`.

  **Expected errors**:
  - `401 unauthorized` — missing/invalid/expired bearer token.
  - `409 already_in_another_room` — this player already owns/joined a room
    that hasn't closed. Close it first (or use the other player's token).
}
